Hello Stephanie,

Please see attached your settlement offer in relation to my employment trib=
unal case against the Royal Sun and Alliance Insurance plc.
Throughout the document, you have provided me with poor and unsolicited leg=
al advice, which has caused me significant detriment. Your advice has encou=
raged me to take the settlement offer of =A310,000 subject to agreed COT3 w=
ording despite my claim amounting to =A336,723,194 (Thirty-six million, sev=
en hundred twenty-three thousand, one hundred ninety-four pounds).
My claim includes reimbursement of legal fees and a suggestion to the court=
 that the respondent should be fined. Had I followed your advice, of which =
I never asked, I would have faced a loss of =A336,713,194 in claims award, =
reimbursement of legal fees, and the respondent would have unfairly avoided=
 a court-imposed fine.

You are aware I am representing myself and that I have a disability. Pinsen=
t Masons LLP on the other hand are a massive legal firm with over 400 partn=
ers.

Of course, I will be raising this to the SRA and the tribunal. However, the=
 purpose of this email is to give you the opportunity to address and rectif=
y this issue directly. This matter is separate from the tribunal proceeding=
s.

To resolve this, I am suggesting that Pinsent Masons make a payment of =A33=
6,713,194 to me.

I am providing you until the 26th of March 2025 5pm to respond.

Kind regards,
Abdul Alim

